on the edge of its hume in a forest the  grim reality of war  nestled between the trees graves of  those who died during the russian  occupation of the city  each has a story at the moment unknown  ukraine says some of the bodies exhumed  show signs of torture  we are here at a place where you can see  three graves in the first one there's a  rope on the neck and the hands are tied  on some bodies we see traces of torture  the burial site was discovered after the  russians left a few days ago police say  they are mostly civilians but bodies of  17 ukrainian soldiers were pulled out of  a mass grave on the edge of the burial  site  investigators and forensic experts are  already at work there are hundreds of  graves here in the forest some of them  are marked and appear to even have the  date of death but there are many others  that are just numbered  sergey came to identify some of them  46 of his neighbors died in the  airstrike that targeted his building  he pulled their bodies out of the rubble  people had to pay for the burial and if  you didn't have money then they were  buried with a number  sometimes they put signs like woman with  a red coat those who were burying were  maybe local fixers russians and  separatists from donetsk and luhansk  russia invaded itsum in the early days  of the war  it was used as a logistical hub to  supply its forces in the donbas  it's now a city in ruins desolate  there's no power water or gas  ukrainian soldiers are back on the  streets but tatiana wonders how she's  going to face the approaching winter she  says some people froze to death alone in  their homes at the beginning of the war  sitting on the bench nearby olga says  most of the death happened  i can say it's a mass grave people bury  their dead anywhere they could in their  gardens and squares the russian mayor  then send a team to exhume the bodies  from around the city and took them near  the cemetery she's hoping to find her  husband who also died in an airstrike 